From d7b4c4cdccc4cb4a82a389c927883059383efb49 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 07:30:50 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(kanban): carry failed-result evidence through the Board
 release [daveey]

Main's failed-result observer closes the run locally and records worker_output/source_result_event_uid on the crashed event. On a Board-primary card our run-scoped release owns that closure, so the classifier payload now rides the release as 'diagnostic' (the Board puts it on its one outcome event), the observer stops waiting once a release is queued, and the core fake Board models release ops like transitions.ts. Explicit allow_nested for main's composable transactions in receipt tests.
---
 .../kanban_db_dispatch_crash_accounting.py    |  9 ++--
 hermes_cli/kanban_failed_result_observer.py   |  5 ++
 hermes_cli/kanban_failure_accounting.py       |  7 ++-
 tests/hermes_cli/kanban_sync_fake_board.py    | 49 ++++++++++++++++++-
 .../test_kanban_failed_result_sync.py         |  6 ++-
 .../test_kanban_local_failure_receipt.py      |  4 +-
 6 files changed, 70 insertions(+), 10 deletions(-)

